Third-party programs in the Stepclimb server image
==================================================

The Stepclimb server (/usr/local/bin/stepclimb) is free software under the GNU Affero General
Public License, version 3 or later; its source is https://github.com/Vainnor/stepclimb at the tag
of the image's version. The image also holds these separate programs, which the server runs as
child processes to transcode uploaded videos. Each keeps its own license.

  /usr/local/bin/ffmpeg, /usr/local/bin/ffprobe
      FFmpeg 9.0.2 and the libraries linked into it, built statically by the
      static-ffmpeg project. GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
      License text: common-licenses/GPL-3. Source: ffmpeg/SOURCE.

  /usr/local/bin/prlimit, /usr/lib/<triplet>/libsmartcols.so.1*
      util-linux 2.38.1 from Debian 12 (bookworm), packages util-linux and
      libsmartcols1, version 2.38.1-5+deb12u3. prlimit is under the GNU General
      Public License, version 2 or later, libsmartcols under the GNU Lesser General
      Public License, version 2.1 or later. Copyright and license details:
      util-linux/copyright and util-linux/libsmartcols1.copyright; license texts in
      common-licenses/. Source: util-linux/SOURCE.

The other files of the base image (gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian12) are Debian packages whose
copyright files are in /usr/share/doc.

docs/adr/0035-ffmpeg-in-the-image.md in the Stepclimb repository records why these programs
are here and how their licenses fit the server's.
